   "shape_m": "p",
   "html_text": "Consider proposition ⟦M⟧ constituting the conclusion of an argument having proposition ⟦M⟧ as premise (where ⟦M⟧ can be a set or conjunction of propositions). If ⟦M⟧ is justified for a subject ⟦M⟧ by evidence ⟦M⟧ , this justification may transmit to ⟦M⟧ if ⟦M⟧ is aware of the entailment between ⟦M⟧ and ⟦M⟧ . When this happens, ⟦M⟧ is justified for ⟦M⟧ in virtue of her justification for ⟦M⟧ based on ⟦M⟧ and her knowledge of the inferential relation from ⟦M⟧ to ⟦M⟧ . Consider this example from Wri",
